  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are clear at this time across\nnorthern and central Nevada this morning. This is due to an upper\nlevel ridge sitting over southern Nevada and will be slowly \nmoving east today. The feature is forecast to remain over the \nsouthwestern United States through the upcoming weekend. High \ntemperatures this afternoon and through the weekend will \ngenerally be in the 80s. with lows in the 40s. Record to near \nrecord high temperatures are possible across all five climate \nlocations for the upcoming weekend.\n\nHeights will fall slightly as a weak upper trough tries to work\nits way east on Monday. Slightly cooler temperatures expected for\nthat afternoon, but highs will still be well above normal with \nparts of northern Nevada seeing near record temperatures. Tuesday \nand through the rest of the week, temperatures remain mainly in \nthe 70s and 80s for northern and central Nevada with lows in the \n40s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM\ngrids at this time. High confidence continues with the \nunseasonably warm temperatures Friday and over the weekend. \nHigh confidence with respect to the above normal temperatures \nthrough next week.",
